  "reason": "With no prior evidence (experiment 1 of 10), the priority is to establish a strong performance baseline while reducing uncertainty about the overall architecture. I select config_044 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) because it combines the most expressive choices across all design dimensions: both modalities (multimodal), multiple profiles per cell (multiprofile), a learned foundation-model RNA encoder (scgpt), the strongest image backbone (ViT-L), the most flexible aggregation (transformer), and a learnable fusion (weighted). If this configuration performs well, it gives a high bar to beat and I can ablate individual components in subsequent experiments to identify which choices drive performance. If it underperforms, it reveals that the combination of all 'maximal' choices is suboptimal, redirecting exploration toward simpler or alternative encoders/aggregations. This single experiment simultaneously tests the core hypothesis that multimodal + multiprofile + learned encoders + transformer aggregation is a strong regime, maximizing information gain per experiment under the tight 10-experiment budget."
